## Rule 1: Only Change What I Ask
- Only edit the exact files, components, functions, or lines I explicitly mention.
- Do not modify or remove unrelated code, logic, features, or UI components.
- When I say “modify the interface,” it means adjust styling only, unless I say otherwise.

## Rule 2: Preserve Functionality
- Do not remove or disable any existing buttons, tabs, or features unless I say "delete".
- Keep all current imports, functions, endpoints, and structure unchanged unless specified.
- Do not rename variables, functions, or files unless I ask.

## Rule 3: Confirm Before Risky Changes
- If a change might affect multiple parts of the system, ask for confirmation before applying it.
- If unsure about my request, generate a safe draft or suggest options instead of editing directly.

## Rule 4: UI Changes
- Limit edits to CSS/styling for UI adjustments unless I explicitly request functional changes.
- Do not remove or change tab/page navigation elements.
- Preserve all existing buttons and controls.

## Rule 5: Transparency
- Always explain what changes were made and why.
- Never refactor unrelated parts of the project unless I explicitly say so.
- If deletion is required, wrap the removed code in comments first for my review.
